\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, it belongs not to my care
\par Whether I die or live;
\par To love and serve Thee is my share,
\par And this Thy grace must give.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. If life be long, I will be glad
\par That I may long obey;
\par If short, yet why should I be sad
\par To soar to endless day?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Christ leads me through no darker
\par rooms
\par Than he went through before;
\par He that into God's kingdom comes
\par Must enter by this door.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Come, Lord, when grace has made
\par me meet
\par Thy blessed face to see;
\par For if Thy work on earth be sweet,
\par What will Thy glory be?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then shall I end my sad complaints,
\par And weary, sinful days,
\par And join with the triumphant saints
\par That sing Jehovah's praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. My knowledge of that life is small,
\par The eye of faith is dim;
\par But 'tis enough that Christ knows all,
\par And I shall be with Him.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

